Dear Koichi,

Could you review the attached questions and denominator table before our consultation on 18 July? The low-dose observational study plans 48 participants to assess whether the planned items can be recorded and where recording stops. It is not intended to establish an effect.

In our earlier table, an entered zero, an unrecorded value within scope and a blank outside scope all appeared as zero. We could not recover the item denominator or the reason for an absent record from that display. The 14 June table proposes a separate denominator and missing-reason rows for each item; its count cells are still blank. Please start with each item's eligibility condition and unit, then read the target, recorded and missing-reason columns.

The PDF sets out twelve questions, including the treatment of recorded zero and unresolved reasons. If any points in the reason fields are difficult to judge, could you let me know by 12 July? That will help us prepare for the discussion on the 18th.

Thank you for your help.

Best regards,
Mitsuko Suzuki
Katsuragawa Clinical Research Center

